Answer: Yes. According to the Philadelphia Inquirer, on Friday, October 23, 2020, the Union League Legacy Foundation placed bright-red "BALLOT BOX" signs on two trash cans in Philadelphia—at Broad and Sansom Streets and 15th and Sansom Streets—as an advertisement for an exhibit on the history of voting rights. The signs were removed within a couple of hours after the foundation realized they could mislead voters into thinking a trash can was an official ballot box.

